  "detail": null,
  "summary": "I worked through all 7 patients on the DOAC dose review list (week of 10/19/2026) under RBC-PHARM-07. Five apixaban or rivaroxaban doses changed and two stayed the same. Each patient has a signed progress note with the values used and the records cited.\n\nFinal doses:\n- **Irene Castellano (pt-0061), apixaban: 2.5 → 5 mg twice daily (mr-t0001).** She was on 2.5 mg because of itraconazole. The St. Brigid infectious disease letter of 9/10 says that course ended 8/14. She meets none of the 3 dose criteria (age 74, 78 kg, SCr 1.02).\n- **Frank Delgado (pt-0003), rivaroxaban: no net change, 20 mg daily.** I first lowered it to 15 mg (mr-t0003) based on St. Brigid's 10/19 creatinine of 160 µmol/L. During the review the lab corrected that value to 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL) after an analyzer fault. With the corrected value his creatinine clearance (CrCl) is 59.9, so I put 20 mg back (mr-t0011) and wrote a correction note.\n- **Raymond Duquette (pt-0041), apixaban: 5 → 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0005).** He meets none of the dose criteria, but takes itraconazole (active order mr-00359 from Dr. Sorensen). Itraconazole was not changed.\n- **Norman Fairweather (pt-0062), apixaban: no change, 5 mg twice daily.** St. Brigid ED creatinines arrived during the review: 150 µmol/L on 10/21, then 100 µmol/L (1.13 mg/dL) on 10/22. Using the latest, only the age criterion (82) is met. I wrote a short note.\n- **Eugene Moravec (pt-0038), rivaroxaban: 15 → 20 mg daily (mr-t0007).** The 5/2026 reduction used ideal body weight; the policy requires actual weight. With 96 kg and SCr 1.45, CrCl is 56.1. He later sent a portal message giving a home-scale weight of 185 lb (about 84 kg). The policy doesn't count patient-reported weights, so the dose stays.\n- **Marjorie Pellegrino (pt-0043), rivaroxaban: 20 → 15 mg daily (mr-t0013).** On the 10/07 creatinine her dose was correct. A new creatinine of 1.25 on 10/22 arrived during the review, which gives CrCl 43.6 (female, 75, 71 kg).\n- **Harold Vance (pt-0002), apixaban: no net change, 2.5 mg twice daily.** I first raised it to 5 mg (mr-t0009): he now meets only the age criterion (82, 64.9 kg, SCr 1.21), and the earlier reduction dated from his February kidney injury. A St. Brigid dermatology letter then arrived saying itraconazole 200 mg daily started 10/22 for 12 weeks. I went back to 2.5 mg (mr-t0012) and wrote a correction note. Itraconazole was not added or changed.\n\n**Inbox:** I closed the 4 result and document items for pt-0003, pt-0062, pt-0043 and pt-0002, linking each to its order or note. Mr. Moravec's portal message (inbox-a0003) is still open for you to answer. No other new items came in, and I didn't touch your other inbox items.\n\n**For your attention:**\n- **Mr. Moravec:** if a clinic weight confirms about 84 kg, his CrCl drops to about 49 and the policy dose becomes 15 mg. I'd suggest weighing him at his next visit.\n- **Mr. Vance:** please re-review his apixaban dose when the itraconazole course ends, around 1/14/2027.\n- **Patients not notified:** I didn't message any patients about their dose changes.",
